    "## The core rule: the vsim measurement window (ROI) is very narrow\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the single most important limitation. Everything in Tier 1 is a\n",
    "consequence of it.\n",
    "\n",
    "When execution hands off to vsim, the resume step writes back only a small\n",
    "part of the CPU state. Read `resume_driver.hpp`: it restores GPRs,\n",
    "FPRs, the V registers, PC, the writable M-mode CSRs - `mstatus`, `mtvec`,\n",
    "`mcycle`, `minstret`, `fcsr` (since L20, 2026-06-12), `mscratch`\n",
    "(since L23, 2026-06-15), and `mepc`/`mcause`/`mtval`/`mie`/`mip`\n",
    "(since L24, 2026-06-15) - plus, since\n",
    "L6 (2026-06-13), the privilege level via `dcsr.prv` (write-verified) and,\n",
    "for S/U-privilege handoffs only, the PMP block.\n",
    "It does NOT write `satp`, `medeleg`, `mideleg` - S-mode CSRs the\n",
    "M-only default engine does not implement - and for M-mode\n",
    "handoffs PMP stays unrestored too (L2).\n",
    "\n",
    "The cell below prints the complete CSR list the resume driver knows. Note\n",
    "what is still missing: no `satp`, `medeleg`, `mideleg` (S-mode CSRs the\n",
    "M-only default engine lacks). `mip` is restored but not `--verify`d (its\n",
    "pending bits are hardware-driven)."
   ]
