    "## State coverage: what the wire format carries\n",
    "\n",
    "Inventory view of the ROI rule above. Everything below is checked against\n",
    "`include/hybrid/state_abi.h` (struct), the QEMU plugin drain\n",
    "(`qemu_plugin/hybrid_handoff.c`), the vsim resume (`resume_driver.hpp`),\n",
    "and the vsim drain (`state_drain.hpp`).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Carried in `hybrid_state_v1`\n",
    "\n",
    "- 32 GPRs, 32 FPRs\n",
    "- `fcsr` (frm + sticky fflags; added 2026-06-12, closing L20)\n",
    "- 13 M-mode CSRs: `mstatus, mepc, mtvec, mcause, mtval, mscratch,\n",
    "  medeleg, mideleg, mip, mie, mcycle, minstret, satp`\n",
    "- PMP: 16 `pmpcfg` + 64 `pmpaddr`\n",
    "- V extension: `vstart, vtype, vl, vlenb, vreg[32], vxsat, vxrm, vcsr`\n",
    "- F13 warmup metadata: `mcycle_at_measure_start`, `minstret_at_measure_start`\n",
    "- `reserved[208]` = room for ~26 more `uint64` (wire format is version 2\n",
    "  since L11 widened `vreg[]` to 128 bytes per register)\n",
    "\n",
    "### NOT in the wire format at all\n",
    "\n",
    "- All S-mode CSRs: `stvec, sepc, scause, stval, sscratch, sie, sip,\n",
    "  scounteren, senvcfg, stimecmp`\n",
    "- HPM block: `mhpmcounter3..31`, `mhpmevent3..31`, `mcounteren,\n",
    "  menvcfg, mcountinhibit, mconfigptr, misa, time`\n",
    "- Every Andes-custom CSR (`mmsc_cfg, mcache_ctl, mmisc_ctl, micm_cfg,\n",
    "  mdcm_cfg, mxstatus, mdcause, mnvec`, ...). See L21.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Carried but NOT restored into vsim\n",
    "\n",
    "The QEMU1 plugin drains them into the struct, but `ResumeDriver`\n",
    "writes none of them into the vsim hart. They are dead during the ROI:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `satp` (L3) and `medeleg, mideleg` (L4) -- S-mode CSRs the M-only\n",
    "  default engine does not implement. (`mscratch` left this set in L23;\n",
    "  `mepc / mcause / mtval / mie / mip` left it in L24 -- all writable\n",
    "  M-mode CSRs that round-trip now.) PMP is restored only for\n",
    "  S/U-privilege handoffs (L6, 2026-06-13) -- without it an S/U ROI\n",
    "  cannot fetch on a PMP-implementing core; M-mode handoffs keep PMP\n",
    "  pass-through-only.\n",
    "\n",
    "CSRs actually restored into vsim: `mstatus, mtvec, mscratch (L23),\n",
    "mepc, mcause, mtval, mie, mip (L24), mcycle, minstret, fcsr`, plus\n",
    "`dcsr.prv` (the privilege level, verified after write) and the PMP block\n",
    "for S/U handoffs (`resume_driver.hpp`). The writable M-mode CSRs are\n",
    "re-read at drain and compared by `--verify`, except `mip` (restored +\n",
    "re-read but not compared -- its pending bits are hardware-driven and\n",
    "diverge between the engines' clocks).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Transport ceiling - why \"all CSRs\" is not free\n",
    "\n",
    "Three surfaces, three ceilings:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Surface         | Mechanism                                     | Ceiling |\n",
    "|-----------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------|\n",
    "| QEMU1 drain     | plugin reads by NAME from gdbstub XML         | only CSRs the QEMU fork advertises |\n",
    "| vsim resume     | DMI Abstract Cmd + Program Buffer (by number) | RO / WARL / locked bits will not take arbitrary values |\n",
    "| vsim drain      | DMI Abstract read (by number)                 | general for any readable CSR |\n",
    "\n",
    "Two structural blockers to \"all CSRs\":\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Wire format is a fixed C struct; `reserved[208]` fits about 26 more\n",
    "   `uint64`. Reaching the full M + S + HPM + Andes set needs a v2 layout.\n",
    "2. Semantics, not just bits. Restore order and side effects already bite\n",
    "   (`mstatus.FS/VS` gating, `vsetvl` atomicity for `vtype/vl`). Writing\n",
    "   `satp` flushes the TLB; Andes `mcache_ctl / mmisc_ctl` toggle caches,\n",
    "   prefetchers, branch prediction and may be RO or locked when written\n",
    "   via the debug module mid-run. Those are exactly the CSRs that shape\n",
    "   the cycle figure.\n",
    "\n",
    "Verdict: extending the wire format to a bounded set in this way is\n",
    "feasible - the L20 fix is the worked example (one `uint64` carved from\n",
    "`reserved[]`, drained by name, restored via the existing\n",
    "abstract-or-PB write, read back at drain). S-mode trap CSRs and a\n",
    "chosen Andes microarch subset can follow the same recipe.\n",
    "\"All RISC-V CSRs including Andes-specific\" is not feasible without\n",
    "redesigning the wire format and lifting the entire ROI envelope (L2-L6)."
   ]
  },
