    "## Tier 1 - Will break on the next real workload\n",
    "\n",
    "### L1. No semihosting inside the ROI; vplat is the supported I/O path  (F-T1.1)\n",
    "\n",
    "- When it bites: any C code calling `printf`, `malloc`, `_exit`, `fopen`, or\n",
    "  anything that ends up in `libgloss` between `enter_vsim()` and\n",
    "  `exit_vsim()`, when linked against a semihosting runtime (`-lgloss_vh`)\n",
    "  instead of the shipped vplat runtime.\n",
    "- What happens: libgloss emits the semihosting magic triple\n",
    "  (`slli x0,x0,0x1f; ebreak; srai x0,x0,0x7`). vsim has no semihosting\n",
    "  handler, so the ebreak traps, the trap handler calls `_exit`, which is\n",
    "  another ebreak -> infinite trap loop -> the run times out.\n",
    "- Where: `docs/vsim_semihosting_investigation.md` (unsolved);\n",
    "  `runtime/{trap.S,handler.c}` (the semihosting runtime).\n",
    "- Status: RESOLVED IN-TREE (2026-06-12). The vplat runtime\n",
    "  (`build/runtime/libandes_sim_runtime.a`, sources in `runtime/`, link with\n",
    "  `-B build/runtime -specs=andes-sim.specs`) routes stdio to UART2, exit to\n",
    "  SimControl, and file io to HTIF -- MMIO devices both engines model -- so\n",
    "  `printf` / `exit` / `fopen` inside the ROI work on fast, cycle AND hybrid\n",
    "  (see USER_GUIDE section 5; smoke tests in `tests/vplat/`). Every C fixture\n",
    "  in the repo now links it (`tests/fixtures/Makefile`); nothing in-tree\n",
    "  uses `-lgloss_vh` anymore, and the plugin's drain-at-exit record became\n",
    "  context-free so the SimPoint profile pass works with the SimControl exit\n",
    "  path (`tests/plugin/test_plugin_drain_at_exit.sh`). The limitation\n",
    "  survives only for EXTERNAL binaries linked with a semihosting libgloss:\n",
    "  there the old rule stands -- keep all I/O in phase 1 (the QEMU leg,\n",
