    "### L2. PMP protection is not carried into vsim for M-mode handoffs  (F-T1.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "- When it bites: an M-mode workload that relies on PMP-enforced memory\n",
    "  regions (write-protect, execute-lock, locked entries) inside the ROI.\n",
    "- What happens: the QEMU plugin drains all 16 `pmpcfg` + 64 `pmpaddr`\n",
    "  entries, but an M-mode resume writes none of them back. vsim runs the\n",
    "  ROI with zeroed PMP, so any protection from phase 1 silently disappears.\n",
    "- Partial since L6 (2026-06-13): an S/U-privilege resume DOES mirror the\n",
    "  producer's PMP block (all 64 `pmpaddr`, then the 8 even `pmpcfg`;\n",
    "  tolerant writes, entries beyond what the hart implements no-op),\n",
    "  because with PMP implemented and no matching entry every S/U access\n",
    "  faults - an S/U ROI could not even fetch without it.\n",
    "- Where: `resume_driver.hpp` - the mirror is gated on `state.priv != 3`.\n",
    "- Status: PARTIAL (open for M-mode handoffs; locked-entry semantics\n",
    "  untested).\n",
    "\n",
    "### L3. Virtual memory (paging) is off inside the ROI\n",
    "\n",
    "- When it bites: any workload running with paging enabled (satp != 0), i.e.\n",
    "  almost anything under an OS.\n",
    "- What happens: `satp` is drained into the state file, but the resume step\n",
    "  never writes `satp` into vsim. The ROI executes in bare mode, so every\n",
    "  virtual address is treated as physical. Loads/stores hit the wrong memory.\n",
    "- Where: `resume_driver.hpp:34-44` (CSR constant list has no satp);\n",
    "  `resume()` never writes it.\n",
    "- Status: OPEN.\n",
    "\n",
    "### L4. Trap / exception state is lost across the ROI  (F-T1.4)\n",
    "\n",
    "- When it bites: any trap (illegal instruction, page fault, misaligned\n",
    "  access, ebreak) fires inside the ROI.\n",
    "- What happens: at drain, `mcause`, `mtval`, `mepc` are NOT re-read from\n",
    "  vsim; the stale QEMU1 values pass straight through into the drained state\n",
    "  file. Any trap-diagnostic logic reading that state sees wrong values.\n",
    "  Also `mepc`/trap-delegation CSRs are not restored into vsim, so trap\n",
    "  handling inside the ROI starts from reset values.\n",
    "- Where: `state_drain.hpp:73-111` (`drain_with_passthrough` re-reads GPRs,\n",
    "  FPRs, V-CSRs, mcycle, minstret - but not mcause/mtval/mepc).\n",
    "- Status: OPEN.\n",
    "\n",
    "### L5. Atomics (LR/SC) cannot cross the handoff  (F-T1.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "- When it bites: an `lr.{w,d}` retires before the trigger and the matching\n",
    "  `sc.{w,d}` retires after it - or any reservation held across the boundary.\n",
    "- What happens: the LR/SC reservation is not part of the wire format, so it\n",
    "  never round-trips. The `sc` always fails on re-entry; a\n",
    "  `__atomic_compare_exchange` loop spins forever.\n",
    "- Where: `include/hybrid/state_abi.h` - no reservation field.\n",
    "- Status: OPEN. The plan is to reject (not transport) a pending reservation\n",
    "  at the trigger.\n",
    "\n",
    "### L20. FP rounding mode (fcsr) does not round-trip  (new 2026-05-28)\n",
    "\n",
    "- When it bit: any workload that sets a non-default rounding mode\n",
    "  (`frm != 0 / RNE`) before the ROI, or relies on sticky `fflags` after\n",
    "  it, while running FP code inside. `fcsr` (which packs `frm[7:5]` and\n",
    "  `fflags[4:0]`) was not in `hybrid_state_v1`, so vsim ran the ROI with\n",
    "  the reset value (RNE, no flags): FP results inside the ROI used the\n",
    "  wrong rounding, and sticky flags after the ROI were wrong.\n",
    "- Status: RESOLVED (2026-06-12). `fcsr` now round-trips end to end,\n",
    "  gated on `HYBRID_FLAG_FP`:\n",
    "  - wire format: `uint64_t fcsr` carved from `reserved[]`\n",
    "    (`state_abi.h`; offset locked by `state_abi_check.h`; pre-fix state\n",
    "    files read back 0 = the old reset-value behavior, so no version bump);\n",
    "  - QEMU1 drain: the plugin reads the `fcsr` gdbstub register alongside\n",
    "    the FPRs (`hybrid_handoff.c`);\n",
    "  - vsim resume: written via the abstract-or-PB CSR path right after the\n",
    "    FPRs, under the same `mstatus.FS` enable (`resume_driver.hpp`);\n",
    "  - vsim drain: re-read into the drained file, and `--verify` /\n",
    "    `state-diff` now compare it (`state_drain.hpp`,\n",
    "    `driver/state_diff.cpp`).\n",
    "  Proven by `tests/fixtures/rt_c_fcsr.c` (frm=RTZ + sticky NX set before\n",
    "  the enter marker, in-ROI self-check, distinct sentinel captured at the\n",
    "  exit drain) - run via `tests/hybrid/e2e_fcsr_roundtrip.sh` and the\n",
    "  regular marker/pc e2e suite (`scripts/run_e2e.sh`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": "### L23. mscratch (M-mode software scratch CSR) did not round-trip  (new 2026-06-15)\n\n- When it bit: any bare-metal, trap-free, single-privilege ROI -- the\n  envelope cell-5 calls *supported* -- that used `mscratch` (CSR 0x340)\n  across the handoff. `mscratch` is the M-mode software scratch register, a\n  side-effect-free read/write CSR; using it needs no trap, no interrupt,\n  no paging. It was drained by QEMU1 but never restored into vsim and never\n  re-read at drain, so:\n  1. a value stashed before the ROI read back as the vsim reset value\n     inside the ROI (the **resume gap**); and\n  2. a value written inside the ROI was dropped from the drained state,\n     which silently kept QEMU1's pre-ROI value (the **drain gap**).\n  `--verify` could not catch (2): `state_diff` excluded `mscratch` as a\n  \"passthrough CSR\". The repo's own guard (`rt_csr_survival.S`) had gone\n  dead in the 2-phase redesign (its readback `phase_c` sat after the exit\n  marker, on the deleted QEMU2 leg), so nothing flagged the regression.\n- Why it mattered: this broke a workload sitting ENTIRELY inside the\n  \"safe\" envelope, so that envelope list was incomplete.\n- Status: RESOLVED (2026-06-15). `mscratch` round-trips end to end:\n  - vsim resume: restored via the tolerant CSR write right after `mtvec`\n    (`resume_driver.hpp`); no FP/V gate -- it is plain M-mode state.\n  - vsim drain: re-read from the hart in `drain_with_passthrough`, so an\n    in-ROI write is captured (`state_drain.hpp`).\n  - `--verify`: `state_diff` strictly compares `mscratch` in the hybrid\n    policy (still excluded in lock-step, where it is reset-vs-reset like\n    `mstatus`/`mtval`).\n  - guard: `tests/fixtures/rt_csr_survival.S` revived as a live 2-phase\n    self-check; unit cases in `resume_driver.test.cpp`,\n    `state_drain.test.cpp`, `state_diff_test.cpp`.\n- Scope: only `mscratch`. The other drained-but-unrestored M-CSRs\n  (`mepc/mcause/mtval/medeleg/mideleg/mip/mie`, `satp`) are trap / interrupt\n  / paging machinery, deferred to the L3/L4 envelope work; `mtvec` is\n  restored but still not re-drained.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
