   "source": [
    "### L24. Writable M-mode trap/interrupt CSRs did not round-trip  (new 2026-06-15)\n",
    "\n",
    "- When it bit: any bare-metal, trap-free, single-privilege ROI -- the\n",
    "  envelope cell-5 calls *supported* -- that used `mepc`, `mcause`,\n",
    "  `mtval`, `mie`, or `mip` across the handoff. These are writable M-mode\n",
    "  CSRs; reading or writing them needs no trap, no interrupt, no paging.\n",
    "  Like `mscratch` before L23, they were drained by QEMU1 but never\n",
    "  restored into vsim and never re-read at drain, so a value stashed\n",
    "  before the ROI read back as the vsim reset value inside it (the\n",
    "  **resume gap**) and a value written inside the ROI was dropped at\n",
    "  drain (the **drain gap**). `--verify` was blind to them too.\n",
    "- The fix (mirrors L23): `ResumeDriver::resume` restores all five via\n",
    "  tolerant abstract writes; `StateDrain::drain_with_passthrough` re-reads\n",
